---
title: "Book a short call with Chris | WhereTo Trips Partner Program"
description: "Pick a time for a 30-minute call with Chris Cupero about the WhereTo Trips Founding Partner program."
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /book-a-call/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
noindex: true
# The Zoho Bookings embed. Leave empty until Chris sends the embed code for the
# "WhereTo Partner Onboarding Call"; then paste ONLY the iframe's src URL here
# (from Zoho Bookings: the service's Share > Embed as iframe). With it empty the
# page shows a placeholder panel that links to the live booking page, so the page
# works either way. See /book-a-call/thanks/ for the after-booking redirect.
bookingSrc: ""
---
{#- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Book a short call — our own page around the Zoho Bookings calendar.

    Why it exists: schedule.wheretotrips.com is Zoho's page, with no Pixel
    and no PostHog, so a click told us someone was curious but never whether
    they booked. Here the calendar is embedded in a page we control, and
    Zoho's after-booking redirect lands on /book-a-call/thanks/, which is
    the only place a "booked" event fires.

    Not linked from anywhere yet. The Texas Partners buttons still go
    straight to schedule.wheretotrips.com (the `schedule` variable at the
    top of TexasPartners.njk); switch that to "/book-a-call/" once the embed
    is in, so the live ad flow never lands on a placeholder.
-#}
{%- set mailto = "mailto:Chris@WhereToTrips.com?subject=Texas%20Partner%20Pilot" -%}
{%- set liveBooking = "https://schedule.wheretotrips.com" -%}

<style>
  /* Page-scoped, narrow-first, widened with min-width queries. */
  .bc-head { padding-top: clamp(28px, 5vw, 56px); }
  .bc-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .bc-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 18px 0 6px; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .bc-meta li {
    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--navy);
    background: var(--azure-tint); border-radius: 999px; padding: 7px 14px;
  }
  .bc-host { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin: 22px 0 6px; }
  .bc-avatar {
    width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background: var(--navy); color: #fff; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: .02em;
  }
  .bc-host strong { display: block; color: var(--navy); font-size: 16px; }
  .bc-host span { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 14px; }
  .bc-cover { margin: 24px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--wg200); }
  .bc-cover li { padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--wg200); }
  .bc-cover h3 { font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .bc-cover p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .bc-email { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .bc-email a { color: var(--azure); font-weight: 600; }

  /* The calendar. The embed and the placeholder share one frame so the
     page does not jump when the real calendar replaces the placeholder. */
  .bc-cal {
    background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--wg200); border-radius: 22px; overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 50px rgba(20, 40, 60, .08); min-height: 640px;
  }
  .bc-cal iframe { display: block; width: 100%; height: 760px; border: 0; }
  .bc-placeholder {
    min-height: 640px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    text-align: center; gap: 14px; padding: 40px 28px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--azure-tint), var(--azure-tint)) padding-box;
  }
  .bc-placeholder .bc-ph-icon { font-size: 60px; line-height: 1; color: var(--azure); }
  .bc-placeholder h3 { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 24px; }
  .bc-placeholder p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 34ch; line-height: 1.6; }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .bc-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); gap: 48px; align-items: start; }
    .bc-side { position: sticky; top: 110px; }
  }
</style>

<section class="block bc-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="bc-grid">
      <div class="bc-side">
        <span class="eyebrow">Texas Founding Partners</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 54px); margin: 0;">Book a short call <span class="italic">with Chris.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 14px;">Thirty minutes to see if the Founding Partner program fits your audience,
          walk through the terms, and answer anything you want to ask.</p>

        <ul class="bc-meta">
          <li>30 minutes</li>
          <li>Phone or video</li>
          <li>No cost, no commitment</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bc-host">
          <div class="bc-avatar" aria-hidden="true">CC</div>
          <div><strong>Chris Cupero</strong><span>Partnerships, WhereTo Trips</span></div>
        </div>

        <ul class="bc-cover">
          <li><h3>Is it a fit?</h3><p>What you cover, who follows you, and how travel fits your content.</p></li>
          <li><h3>The Founding terms</h3><p>30% of what we earn on every trip your followers book, for as long as you stay active.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Next steps</h3><p>If it is a fit, the agreement is signed online and you get your partner code.</p></li>
        </ul>

        <p class="bc-email">Prefer email? <a href="{{ mailto }}">Chris@WhereToTrips.com</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="bc-cal" id="booking">
        {% if bookingSrc %}
          <iframe src="{{ bookingSrc }}" title="Pick a time for your call with Chris" loading="lazy" allow="fullscreen"></iframe>
        {% else %}
          {# Placeholder until the Zoho embed arrives. Still useful: it links to the live
             booking page. data-wt-no-track keeps base.njk's click tracking from counting
             this as a second Lead for someone who already clicked through to this page. #}
          <div class="bc-placeholder">
            <div class="bc-ph-icon">{% icon "calendar" %}</div>
            <h3>The calendar goes here</h3>
            <p>Pick a day and time that works for you. Times are shown in your own time zone.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ liveBooking }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-wt-no-track>See open times</a>
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
